@*
    The router, shared by all three heads.

    AppAssembly is taken off a type in THIS assembly rather than off the entry
    assembly, because the entry assembly differs per head - a MAUI app, a web
    server, a WASM client - and only this one holds the pages.
*@
@*
    THE STORE, STARTED ONCE, ABOVE THE ROUTER. Fluxor needs an initialiser
    somewhere in the tree or the feature states are never seeded: reducers run,
    the store holds its default, and every screen reads an empty conversation
    without a word of complaint. Here rather than in each head's own root for
    the same reason the Router is here - three copies is three chances for one
    to be forgotten, and the one that forgets is a head that silently has no
    memory.
*@
<Fluxor.Blazor.Web.StoreInitializer />

<Router AppAssembly="typeof(Layout.MainLayout).Assembly" NotFoundPage="typeof(Pages.NotFound)">
    <Found Context="routeData">
        <RouteView RouteData="routeData" DefaultLayout="typeof(Layout.MainLayout)" />
        <FocusOnNavigate RouteData="routeData" Selector="h1" />
    </Found>
</Router>
